# Every test file tests/run-tests.sh is allowed to execute, one path per line,
# relative to tests/. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# run-tests.sh still discovers test files by glob; this list is what the glob is
# checked against. The run refuses to start when the two disagree in either
# direction -- a file on disk that nobody listed, or a listed file that is gone.
#
# Why a second list rather than the glob alone: `./tests/run-tests.sh` is
# allow-listed without a prompt in .claude/settings.json, and a glob executes
# whatever it finds. That made writing one file into tests/ enough to run
# anything that file's `deny` and `ask` entries exist to gate -- `podman system
# prune`, the `virsh ... undefine` set, `git push --force`, `sudo` -- with no
# prompt at all. Adding a test file is now a visible, reviewable edit to a
# committed list instead of a silent addition to what an allow-listed command
# executes.
#
# Nothing here is ever run as a path. The entries are compared against the glob
# as text and the glob's own results are what execute, so a line in this file
# cannot become a command.

e2e/test-quickstart-dry-run.sh
test-homebrew-profile.sh
